.SS "int icon_set_state (\fBicon_list\fP * il, \fBicon\fP * icon, icon_state s)"
.PP
change an icon's state. 
.PP
an icon-factory may create elements for all states when the icon is first created; in this case, \fBicon_set_state()\fP needs not be provided. using \fBicon_set_state()\fP does however allow for more flexibility (and reduced use of memory) by creating the desired elements 'on the fly.' 
.PP
\fBReturns:\fP
.RS 4
TRUE if \fBevas_icon_set_state()\fP wrapper show show/hide icon-elements based on their states after calling this, FALSE otherwise. (usually FALSE) 
.RE
.PP
\fBParameters:\fP
.RS 4
\fIil\fP - the icon-list 
.br
\fIicon\fP - the icon in question 
.br
\fIs\fP - the desired state
.RE
.PP

